 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer"><h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What wattage of GaN V charger is needed for fleet and enterprise laptop deployment?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Specify <strong>100W-140W GaN V with PD 3.1 EPR</strong> for fleet deployment. A single 140W charger covers MacBook Pro 16", Dell XPS 15, and ThinkPad P-series at full speed. Dual-port 100W+65W chargers reduce procurement complexity by 50%, one SKU for laptops and phones. <strong>EU laptop USB-C mandate (April 2026) makes GaN V the default for enterprise fleet procurement.</strong></p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer"><h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers verify the factory uses genuine GaN V, not re-labeled GaN III?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Three steps: (1) Request <strong>GaN FET part number</strong> and cross-reference against manufacturer datasheet. (2) Demand <strong>efficiency curves at 230V/50Hz and 115V/60Hz</strong>, GaN V delivers 94-96% vs 90-92% for GaN III. (3) <strong>Thermal test at 100% load for 60 min</strong>, genuine GaN V runs 15-25°C cooler. Request chip procurement invoices from authorized distributors. Navitas offers verification program. WOWOHCOOL provides full FET traceability documentation.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer"><h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the MOQ and lead time for GaN V OEM chargers?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Standard ODM in-stock: <strong>MOQ 500 units.</strong> ODM new-design development: 1,000-2,000. Custom OEM with new tooling: 3,000+. Lead time: 25-35 days after sample approval (ODM in-stock). GaN V component sourcing: 8-12 week lead time, finalize designs 4+ months pre-launch. FOB at 1,000 units: 65W ~$8-11, 100W ~$13-16, 140W ~$16-22. Tiered pricing at 500/1,000/5,000 volumes with full certification docs included.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer"><h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What safety certifications and testing protocols apply to GaN V OEM chargers?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Mandatory:</strong> UL 62368-1 (US), CE LVD+EMC+RoHS (EU), USB-IF PD 3.1. EU: ESPR 2025/2052 (≤0.1W standby, ≥87% efficiency). Quality: 10-layer circuit protection, UL 94 V-0 enclosure rated to 850°C glow wire, <strong>100% 4-hour burn-in at 45°C</strong> (not batch sampling), field failure rate under 0.3% (WOWOHCOOL GaN portfolio ~0.5%, GaN V best-in-class). WOWOHCOOL achieves under 0.3% across millions of units.</p></div>
 
